SWT6621S DKMS package
====================

Install the matching headers for your kernel before installing this package.
On Armbian edge rockchip64, these are linux-headers-edge-rockchip64.
The package builds the SDIO transport, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth modules; it does
not package firmware, a device tree or prebuilt kernel modules.

Module loading, module parameters and board firmware paths are managed by
the distribution or administrator. This package installs no modules-load.d
or modprobe.d configuration. For firmware installed under
/lib/firmware/seekwave, the distribution should set firmware_dir=seekwave.

Packaging targets Debian 11+ and Ubuntu 20.04+. Kernel API compatibility is
separate: matching kernel headers and a supported driver/kernel combination
are required. The architecture-independent package contains source only.

Build on Debian/Ubuntu (older releases provide dh_dkms in dkms):

  sudo apt-get install debhelper dkms build-essential
  # On releases with a separate dh-dkms package, install it as well.
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

Install:

  sudo apt install ./swt6621s-dkms_2026.10.27+git15a66f7_all.deb
  dkms status

Kernel image and header package hooks invoke DKMS automatically. Reinstalling
the same kernel normally reuses an existing DKMS build; a fresh kernel
version requires a new build. Do not remove a running kernel to test this.

The package does not forcibly unload a running driver during installation.
Reboot or reload the three modules to use the newly built modules.

Package versions identify the source snapshot date and Git revision rather
than inventing an upstream release number. Debian packaging-only revisions
can use a trailing .1, .2, etc. in this native package version.
